**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What the Data locations window lists, as data (001 §G 'Every path is overridable in appsettings.json; a Launcher Data locations panel shows them, each with Open folder'; .spec-md §5 `DataLocations`: every path 001 §G names; .spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs`, after `DataLocations` (step 81), each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `DataLocationKind` = `LibraryDatabaseLocation` | `LibraryBackupsLocation` | `PreferencesLocation` | `KitsLocation` | `ExportsLocation` | `CataloguesLocation` | `ShippedCatalogueLocation`, one per field of `DataLocations`, each case documented in one line naming its field; it is never stored, so it has no tag. `static member all : DataLocationKind list` lists them in that order, the order of the record's fields. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryBackupStore.fs`, beside `LibraryDatabase.recreate` (step 87), its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `type LibraryDatabase with static member tryFileOf (connectionString : ConnectionString) : FileName option` reads the connection string through `SqliteConnectionStringBuilder` and answers `None` for an in-memory library (`DataSource` `:memory:` or `Mode` `Memory`) and otherwise `Some` of the `DataSource`'s full path (`Path.GetFullPath`). It is `recreate`'s in-memory test and file read, moved: `recreate` calls it and its own copy is deleted, so one rule says where a library's file is. It touches no file. No other member is added. Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryDatabaseTests.fs` (step 62) gains `tryFileOf answers the library's file, and nothing for an in-memory library`: `Data Source=:memory:` and `Data Source=lib;Mode=Memory;Cache=Shared` answer `None`, and `Data Source=<a folder under the test output>/library.db` answers that file's full path; `recreate`'s facts (step 87) keep their assertions. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/WorkbenchSettingsTests.fs` (step 81) gains `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field`: `DataLocationKind.all` holds the seven cases once each, in the order above.

**Acceptance.** After the location kinds land, `DataLocationKind.all` MUST list the seven 001 §G locations in field order and `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf` MUST be the one rule for a library's file, `recreate` calling it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `tryFileOf answers the library's file, and nothing for an in-memory library` and `every location is a data location kind, in the order of its field`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
